  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WETLANDS RECOVERY IN LAGUNA MADRE &amp; RIO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The decrease in wetlands in the southern part of the Rio Bravo Delta and in Laguna Madre in the state of Tamaulipas has been identified as a significant threat. The project will carry out many activities in this area: &apos;Protection: Protection of 10,546.9 acres of wetlands in the Rio Bravo Delta through a 10-year work plan agreement with the federal protected area, &apos;Area para la Proteccin de Flora and Fauna Laguna Madre y Delta del Ro Bravo&apos;. &apos;Restoration and enhancement: a) Enhancement of 10,546.9 acres of a wetland through the construction and rehabilitation of culverts that will recover hydrological flows; b) Enhancement of 101.27 acres of wetlands through removal of invasive plants; c) &apos;Technical Study&apos; for permitting the wetland restoration; d) Two &apos;Environmental Impact Manifests&apos; for the authorization of restoration activities; e) Management and relocation of wildlife in sites of high wildlife density; f) Solid waste management programs; g) Environmental compensation actions focused on soil and vegetation restoration. &apos;Capacity building: a) Analysis of the landscape dynamics of the Ro Bravo delta; b) Hydrological characterization of a wetland to determine the type and dimensions of culvert rehabilitation; c) Monitoring migratory waterbirds, waterfowl and shorebirds; and d) Biodiversity monitoring in the restoration and influence zones. &apos;Environmental training and education: a) Capacity building among fishermen; b) Communications strategy to disseminate the actions and benefits of the project and promote respect and care for migratory water birds; c) Supervision of environmental programs in the northern zone of Laguna Madre .</narrative>
  </description>
